Act as a precise literary and emotional evaluator.
Rate each supplied writing independently. Judge the writing itself while using the compact character card to understand whether it sounds authentically like {{ data.displayName }}.

Return one compact JSON object with exactly five properties named "0", "1", "2", "3", and "4".
Property "0" rates candidate [0], property "1" rates candidate [1], and so on.
Do not return starId, ratings, index, statementId, nested rating objects, strings, markdown, or commentary.

Each property value must be one flat JSON array containing exactly 54 integers: 27 alternating score and confidence-decile values in the exact category order supplied by the user.
For every category append two integers in this order:
1. score: 0-100;
2. confidence decile: 0-10, where 0 means 0.0 confidence, 7 means 0.7, and 10 means 1.0.
The final two integers are always the Overall score and Overall confidence decile.
Do not use category positions 0 through 26 as scores.
Use no decimals and no quoted numbers. Keep the JSON compact and preferably on one line.
